# Published artifacts are verified BYTE FOR BYTE.
#
# The default `* text=auto` this repository started with normalises line
# endings on checkout, which would change the bytes a client hashes without
# changing anything in the commit — and the failure surfaces as a SHA-256
# mismatch, i.e. as a tampering alarm rather than as a checkout setting. That
# is the worst possible way to learn about a git configuration.
#
# Everything the channel serves is therefore declared binary-exact.
*.json      -text
*.jsonl     -text
*.sig       -text

# Prose stays ordinary text.
*.md        text
.gitattributes text
